\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Domain overlap heatmap showing the Szymkiewicz--Simpson overlap coefficient of shared terminology between each pair of Ento-Linguistic domains. Darker cells indicate higher overlap; Power \& Labor exhibits the strongest cross-domain connectivity (particularly to Behavior \& Identity and Sex \& Reproduction), while Economics shows zero bridging terms with other domains. Off-diagonal asymmetry reflects directional borrowing patterns. Values are computed at runtime from the extracted term-domain assignments in \colorbox {codebg}{\color  {codefg}\ttfamily  output/data/domain\_statistics.json}.}}{15}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:domain_overlap}{{3}{15}{Domain overlap heatmap showing the Szymkiewicz--Simpson overlap coefficient of shared terminology between each pair of Ento-Linguistic domains. Darker cells indicate higher overlap; Power \& Labor exhibits the strongest cross-domain connectivity (particularly to Behavior \& Identity and Sex \& Reproduction), while Economics shows zero bridging terms with other domains. Off-diagonal asymmetry reflects directional borrowing patterns. Values are computed at runtime from the extracted term-domain assignments in \texttt {output/data/domain\_statistics.json}}{figure.caption.5}{}}
